\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar sheds gains as market seeks clues on economy. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Yonggi Kang \par \uc2 572 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juli 2003\par 08:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, July 17 (Reuters) - The dollar was flat on Thursday, falling from the day's high against the yen as dealers sought more clues on the future of the U.S. economy following Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan's congressional testimony. \par \par \uc2  The dollar rose to a session high of 118.27 yen in the morning thanks to buying by European and Japanese trust banks. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the greenback was boosted by falling Tokyo stocks and news that South Korea had exchanged machinegun fire with North Korea in the demilitarised zone. But by late afternoon, the dollar was quoted at levels almost unchanged from Wednesday's close in New York because its upside was capped by offers from Japan's exporters and any falls were supported by fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "If you sell the dollar, there's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . If you buy the dollar, the upside is capped," said a Japanese trust bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  The second leg of Greenspan's congressional testimony on Wednesday failed to offer incentives as he largely reiterated what he had said the previous day. \par \par \uc2  Greenspan said the U.S. economy was recovering, but vowed the Fed would remain vigilant on deflation. \par \par \uc2  "Dealers want to see more U.S. indicators to assess whether the economic recovery is for real," said Kouki Muroi, deputy manager of the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading group at Aozora Bank. \par \par \uc2  "Right now, expectations are getting ahead of reality." \par \par \uc2  At 0605 GMT, the dollar was quoted at 118.06/11 yen compared with Wednesday's late U.S. level of 118.07/15. \par \par \uc2  DOLLAR STILL BULLISH \par \par \uc2  The shooting on the Korean peninsula was between observation posts on either side of the demarcation line at the heart of the DMZ. \par \par \uc2  South Korea will carry out an investigation and based on the results would determine the next step, said Colonel Lee Hong-ki, spokesman for the South's Joint Chiefs of Staff. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said sentiment was more in favour of the dollar than the yen even though that pair would likely continue trading in a 117.50-118.50 yen range for now. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar is highly unlikely to tumble against the yen as the authorities seem to be showing strong commitment to restraining a sharp rise in the yen," said Michihisa Tanimoto, deputy general manager at Sumitomo Life Insurance. \par \par \uc2  "Amid this trend, speculators cannot sell the dollar heavily, which should make it solid from around 117 yen," he said. \par \par \uc2  Japan's top financial diplomat, Zembei Mizoguchi, continued to offer verbal threats, saying on Thursday there was still some volatility in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, and repeated that the Japanese authorities were ready to take all appropriate measures. \par \par \uc2  The market was taking a wait-and-see stance after the greenback fell from a two-month high of $1.1109 hit on Wednesday against the euro. \par \par \uc2  The euro was little changed at $1.1222/27 from its U.S. level of $1.1220/24. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, Bundesbank President Ernst Welteke was quoted as saying he would not bet on any further rate cuts from the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the moment because they would not have any positive economic effect. \par \par \uc2  "It's still tough to buy euros looking both at economic fundamentals and charts," said Sumitomo Life's Tanimoto. \par \par \uc2  "It's more likely the euro will test below $1.1 in the near term," he said. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030717dz7h00cyu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
