\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar consolidating but bull tone intact. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Chikafumi Hodo \par \uc2 466 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juli 2003\par 03:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, July 17 (Reuters) - The dollar was under consolidation pressure on Thursday after rising sharply in recent sessions, but its underlying bullishness stayed intact on brightening prospects for the U.S. economy. \par \par \uc2  The second leg of Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan's congressional testimony on Wednesday failed to offer new incentives as he largely reiterated what he had said the previous day. \par \par \uc2  Greenspan said the U.S. economy was recovering, but vowed the Fed would remain vigilant on deflation. \par \par \uc2  The market was taking a wait-and-see stance after the greenback fell from a two-month high of $1.1109 hit on Wednesday against the euro, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was solid against the yen as the Japanese monetary authorities were thought to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  most recently on Tuesday when it dropped below 117 yen for the first time since late May, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  A rumour circulated that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  during Asian time on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar is highly unlike to tumble against the yen as the authorities seem to be showing strong commitment to restraining a sharp rise in the yen," said Michihisa Tanimoto, deputy general manager at Sumitomo Life Insurance. \par \par \uc2  "Amid this trend, speculators cannot sell the dollar heavily, which should make it solid from around 117 yen," he said. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow said on Wednesday that there was no change in Washington's long-standing policy for a firm dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The policy is we have a strong dollar policy. We believe in a strong dollar," Snow told reporters at the U.S. embassy in London. \par \par \uc2  Japan's top financial diplomat, Zembei Mizoguchi, continued to offer verbal threats, saying on Thursday there was still some volatility in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, and repeated that the Japanese authorities were ready to take all appropriate measures. \par \par \uc2  Still, the greenback faced some selling pressure after Greenspan commented during the question and answer session at Wednesday's testimony on the subject of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying it could not be done indefinitely. \par \par \uc2  At 0105 GMT, the dollar was quoted at 118.12/17 yen compared with Wednesday's late U.S. level of 118.07/15. \par \par \uc2  The euro was little changed at $1.1213/18 from its U.S. level of $1.1220/24, with a wait-and-see mood dominanting. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, Bundesbank President Ernet Welteke was quoted as saying he would not bet on any further rate cuts from the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the moment because they would not have any positive economic effect. \par \par \uc2  "It's still tough to buy euros looking both at economic fundamentals and charts," said Sumitomo Life's Tanimoto. \par \par \uc2  "It's more likely the euro will test below $1.1 in the near term," he said. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030717dz7h003ed\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
