\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -2: Market To Watch US Snow Visit To Europe \b0\par\par\uc2 524 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juli 2003\par 08:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The yen was also underpinned by news that the Bank of Japan upgraded its economic assessment for the first time since July 2002 Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ said uncertainty over the economy is abating slightly and that exports were flat as opposed to weak. But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  maintained caution about the state of the economy going forward due to ongoing uncertainty over the economic recovery overseas, mainly in the U.S. \par \par \uc2  The euro lost more ground in the morning as yen-selling talk pushed up the dollar-yen. The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell to a new three-month low of $1.1115 at 0022 GMT, before short-covering pared losses. \par \par \uc2  Greenspan will make another congressional appearance Wednesday to testify before the Senate Banking Committee. \par \par \uc2  Market participants are also keeping their eyes on another horizon, as U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow is on a four-day visit to the U.K. and Germany to meet with financial officials. \par \par \uc2  Snow told The Times of London in an interview published on the newspaper's website Wednesday that the 12 eurozone countries should take stronger measures to revive their economies. \par \par \uc2  He said he was "very confident" that U.S. growth would accelerate strongly from an annual rate of 3% in the present quarter to "comfortably above 4%" next year, and that the first signs of this were "already beginning to be seen," with improving business confidence, rising profits, a stable dollar, and a big expected influx of foreign investment. \par \par \uc2  And in case European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials had any ideas about following Japan's example if the euro were to retest highs, Snow pre-emptively said that governments should best leave \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to markets. \par \par \uc2  "In America and Europe we have a freely floating competitive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  system and governments that don't believe in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." he said. "If we manage our economies well, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  will take care of themselves." \par \par \uc2  Some Asian strategists wondered how long before such U.S. rumblings against \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in general turn to specific complaints about \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy to keep the yen from strengthening. \par \par \uc2  "The Bush administration wants to see a healthy economic recovery before the (2004 U.S. presidential) election, meaning they need reasonable growth early next year," and might take aim at Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  actions, said Credit Suisse First Boston strategist Satoru Ogasawara. \par \par \uc2  For now, though, he said CSFB will likely maintain its three-month dollar forecast of Y117. \par \par \uc2  "Downward pressure on the dollar remains intact, but as we've seen last night, Japanese authorities will try to maintain the dollar-yen around Y117, and so far they've been succeeding," he said. \par \par \uc2  -By Lisa Twaronite, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; lisa.twaronite@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  -Edited by John Gibson \par \par \uc2  The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly. \par \par \uc2  Subscribers can find this