\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Euro Loses Ground On Schroeder Comments \b0\par\par\uc2  By Lisa Twaronite \par \uc2 751 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juli 2003\par 07:39\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The euro came under pressure in Asia Friday from U.S. and European fund sales after Germany's leader reportedly called for a weaker European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In an interview with the Financial Times reported on the newspaper's Web site, German Chancellor Gerhard Schroeder strongly implied Thursday that the ECB should \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to reduce the value of the euro and help European exporters. \par \par \uc2  "I assume the intelligent people in the leadership of the ECB discuss the question every day of whether they have done enough in the context of the dollar/euro exchange rate to maintain the competitiveness of exports from Europe," Schroeder told the FT. \par \par \uc2  Schroeder has expressed concern about the euro's strength before, but some market participants took the opportunity to take profits on the euro ahead of the weekend, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The euro dropped from its early morning high of $1.1384 at 2155 GMT to as low as $1.1300 at 0200 GMT, before bouncing off options-related support at that level. Against the yen, it fell from a high of Y133.95 to Y133.32. \par \par \uc2  Germany's economy contracted 0.2% in the first quarter of this year from the previous quarter, partly due to weaker export growth. \par \par \uc2  "The Europeans are worried about having all of the dollar adjustment on their side, and are increasing their calls for Asia to revalue," said James Malcolm, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at J.P. Morgan in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "But the actual leverage that Europe has with Asian governments is pretty weak," he said, so in order to stem their single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's appreciation, some European officials think, "if you can't beat them, join them." \par \par \uc2  Since the euro is well off its all-time high of $1.1929 reached May 27, it's "almost a moot discussion now," he added. \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT, the euro was at $1.1326, lower than $1.1382 in New York and $1.1342 in Tokyo. Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y133.53, down from with Y133.85 in New York, though largely unchanged from Y133.55 in Tokyo Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar edged higher against the yen on short-covering, and was quoted at Y117.90, above Y117.60 in New York and Y117.75 in Tokyo late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.6357, compared with $1.6346 in New York and $1.6354 in Tokyo Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Schroeder's reported remarks about euro strength came hours after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its key interest rate at 2%, as market participants had expected. \par \par \uc2  The dollar benefitted from the euro's fall, and ticked higher against the yen in cross-trading, although sales by Japanese exporters kept the dollar from rising above Y118, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  got some support from morning comments from Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa, who said the yen is currently strong with regard to its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  counterparts in view of the nation's purchasing power. \par \par \uc2  "I'm not saying that's good or bad, but that's the current situation," Shiokawa told a regular press conference. He declined to comment on specific \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels or market conditions. \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa has mentioned purchasing power parity on several occasions since late last year, when he declared that the yen, which was trading near Y125 to the dollar at the time, was "too strong," and that a more appropriate level would be Y150. \par \par \uc2  While Shiokawa's comments Friday helped underpin dollar sentiment, they "weren't a big trading factor today," said a dealer at a Japanese bank, as market participants no longer think that Japan has any intention of selling yen to achieve Shiokawa's theoretical levels. \par \par \uc2  But at the same time, traders believe Japan's finance ministry wouldn't hesitate to sell yen to prevent any sharp appreciation. The government has spent some Y7 trillion since the start of the year \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep a strong yen from undermining \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy. \par \par \uc2  -By Lisa Twaronite, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; lisa.twaronite@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  -Edited by Hugh Lawson \par \par \uc2  The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly. \par \par \uc2  Subscribers can find this table: \par \par \uc2  -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087. \par \par \uc2  -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX \par \par \uc2  -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT \par \par \uc2  -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030711dz7b0009n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
