\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr Gains Slightly Against Yen In Thin Trade \b0\par\par\uc2  By Lisa Twaronite \par \uc2 615 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juli 2003\par 07:43\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The dollar ticked higher against the yen and lost a few points against the euro in Asia Thursday, as major \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs stuck to narrow ranges in relatively thin trading. \par \par \uc2  Early in the session, hedge selling pressured the euro ahead of Thursday's policy meeting of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But market consensus is that the bank will stand pat, and that led some U.S. funds to buy back the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the view it may have been oversold in recent sessions. \par \par \uc2  U.S. funds also bought the dollar ahead of the 0100 GMT Tokyo fixing, when Japanese commercial banks set rates for customers, but took profits when the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to clear resistance at Y118. \par \par \uc2  Perceptions that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  would continue its policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb any sharp yen rise put a floor under the dollar above the Y117.50 line of support, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Last month, the ministry sold Y628.9 billion through the Bank of Japan to stem yen appreciation. \par \par \uc2  "The outlook for the Japan economy is improving, which should naturally lead to a stronger yen, if it weren't for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Ryohei Muramatsu, treasury manager at Commerzbank in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y117.75, above Y117.70 in New York, but below Y118.29 in Tokyo late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.1342, higher than $1.1339 in New York and $1.1319 in Tokyo. Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y133.55, compared with Y133.46 in New York and Y133.93 in Tokyo Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.6354, down from $1.6362 in New York, but slightly higher than $1.6352 in Tokyo Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The euro got a boost against both the yen and the dollar toward the end of Asian trading, as Japanese investors joined European funds in buying the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The euro managed to clear Y133.80 resistance on the mostly European-driven gains, bringing Y134 into sight. Against the dollar, the euro broke above $1.1350 to a session high of $1.1365, just a few ticks below Wednesday's high. \par \par \uc2  Japanese investors have poured into eurozone assets in recent months, buying net Y2.3 trillion worth of European assets in the January-April period, according to an estimate by Morgan Stanley. \par \par \uc2  While such investment has continued, fund flows began to favor the yen after Japanese stocks started rising from the 20-year lows they hit in late April. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, the Nikkei 225 Stock Average shed 0.4% to end at 9955.62, but the index is still more than 30% above its April low, as foreign fund managers rebalance their underweight portfolios. \par \par \uc2  However, market participants don't expect the yen to benefit much from those fund flows, as Japan's MOF stands ready to stem its gains with action via the BOJ. \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of Japan will have to keep on going to support the dollar against the yen, which has really blocked trading so far," said Kaneo Ogino, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at HSBC in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  -By Lisa Twaronite, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; lisa.twaronite@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  -Edited by Kirsty Mackenzie \par \par \uc2  The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly. \par \par \uc2  Subscribers can find this table: \par \par \uc2  -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087. \par \par \uc2  -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX \par \par \uc2  -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT \par \par \uc2  -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030710dz7a000ag\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
