\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar pressured vs yen on selling in crosses. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Yonggi Kang \par \uc2 473 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juli 2003\par 03:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, July 10 (Reuters) - The dollar kept a bearish tone against the yen on Thursday, pressured by a weaker Wall Street overnight and buying of yen against other higher-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the euro and Australian dollar. \par \par \uc2  With policy-setting meetings by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Bank of England coming up later in the day, dealers were reluctant to trade actively. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar's bias was on its downside, as gains in stock prices seemed speedier in Tokyo than in New York and latest economic indicators seemed to suggest the Japanese economy was on the recovery path. \par \par \uc2  "Investors are buying back the yen on firmer stocks," said Gen Kawabe, manager of the treasury department at Chuo Mitsui Trust and Banking. \par \par \uc2  "We're seeing some position adjustments in higher-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the Australian dollar and Canadian dollar." \par \par \uc2  At 0031 GMT, the dollar was trading at 117.83/90 yen compared with 117.74/82 in late New York on Wednesday. It fell as low as 117.65 yen in early morning trade. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar's downside was firmly supported by worries about Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and dealers said the dollar's move below 117 yen was unlikely. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.1333/38 against $1.1352/58. \par \par \uc2  The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to slip against the yen, falling to 133.59/66 yen from late New York's 133.75/86 yen. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar fell to 76.98 yen against 77.46 yen. \par \par \uc2  ECB, BOE IN FOCUS \par \par \uc2  Few dealers expect the ECB and the BoE to announce rate cuts at their meetings later in the day. \par \par \uc2  But many players are hesitant to take huge positions ahead of the events due to the slim chance that they might come up with a surprise and on the prospects that the banks may deliver hints of monetary easing in the future. \par \par \uc2  The ECB last cut rates by half a percentage point in June to 2.00 percent. \par \par \uc2  "The market needs to see the results of the ECB meeting so I expect more dealers to remain on the sidelines during Tokyo trading," said a dealer at a Japanese securities firm. \par \par \uc2  On the economic indicator front, data released earlier on Thursday showed the surplus in Japan's current account, the broadest measure of trade in goods and services, rose more than expected in May, helped by a decline in the number of Japanese travelling abroad and by healthy exports to China. \par \par \uc2  The surplus rose 28.5 percent in May from a year earlier to 1.3468 trillion yen ($11.42 billion), the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. Economists in a Reuters poll had forecast a surplus of 1.17 trillion, up 10 percent from the previous year. ($1=117.80 yen). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030710dz7a002h5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
