\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr/Yen Falls As Foreigners Buy Japan Stocks \b0\par\par\uc2  By Ron Harui \par \uc2 626 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juli 2003\par 07:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The dollar fell against the yen in Asia Wednesday as improving sentiment over Japan's economy fueled selling of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by overseas players piling into Japanese stocks. \par \par \uc2  The dollar rose to the mid-Y119s on healthy demand at the Tokyo retail fixing at 0100 GMT, but soon slipped to the low-Y119s as foreign funds sold the U.S. unit for yen to buy Japanese equities. \par \par \uc2  Led by foreign funds' purchases, the benchmark Nikkei 225 Stock Average topped 9,500 for the first time since late September, rising as much as 3.4% at one point. \par \par \uc2  "The Nikkei surged as foreigners apparently bought (stocks) and the yen," said Satoshi Tate, vice president for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at UFJ Bank. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan's "tankan" survey, released Tuesday, was one factor behind foreign funds' buying of Japanese stocks, as it showed an unexpected improvement in business sentiment, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Disappointing overnight U.S. data, in the Institute for Supply Management's manufacturing survey, also weighed on the dollar. Although the ISM reading rose to 49.8 in June, it fell short of expectations of 50.5 and damped growing optimism over the U.S. economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ tankan and the U.S. ISM were a double punch to the dollar/yen's rally," Tate said. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar's slide was limited by expectations Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  may resume its stealth yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid vague talk the ministry has placed covert dollar bids in the low-Y119s. \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y119.33, below Y119.45 late Tuesday in New York. The dollar was at Y119.73 late Tuesday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.1546, lower than $1.1565 late Tuesday in New York. The euro was at $1.1518 in Tokyo Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y137.75, down from Y138.14 in New York late Tuesday. The euro was at Y137.91 in Tokyo late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Trying to jawbone the yen lower early in the session, Japan's Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Zembei Mizoguchi reiterated that there had been no change in the ministry's view that the U.S. economy is stronger than Japan's. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo has maintained that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates should reflect fundamentals, and that such fundamentals don't warrant a strengthening of the yen. \par \par \uc2  Since the beginning of the year, the finance ministry has spent around Y7 trillion on stealth yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent an excessively strong yen from hurting \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's exports and increasing deflationary pressure on the nation's economy. \par \par \uc2  For the rest of the global session, the dollar may consolidate sideways in a narrow Y119.00-Y119.60 range as players are reluctant to trade aggressively ahead of a U.S. employment report due out at 1230 GMT Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The data are expected to provide more clues on whether recent signs of improvement in the U.S. economy are just a flash in the pan or instead herald a longer-term trend. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.6636, up from $1.6632 in New York and higher than $1.6564 in Tokyo Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Ron Harui, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2942; ron.harui@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  -Edited by Kirsty Mackenzie \par \par \uc2  The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly. \par \par \uc2  Subscribers can find this table: \par \par \uc2  -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087. \par \par \uc2  -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX \par \par \uc2  -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT \par \par \uc2  -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030702dz720008s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
