\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -2:  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  June  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Data Later Monday \b0\par\par\uc2 355 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Juni 2003\par 08:59\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Market participants will also be watching the Bank of Japan's quarterly tankan survey scheduled to be released Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Analysts expect the headline sentiment index for large manufacturers to remain at minus 10, the same level as it was in the previous survey in March, showing that managers here remain downbeat. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market participants will also be watching the tankan for clues on companies' \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  expectations. In the last survey, taken in March, large manufacturers predicted an average dollar-yen exchange rate of Y118.03 for the fiscal year through March 2004. \par \par \uc2  Also at 1000 GMT Monday, Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  will announce how much yen it sold in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June, following May's record high Y4 trillion in sales. The ministry is thought to have spent around Y2 trillion in June. \par \par \uc2  But now that the dollar has consolidated in a higher range against the yen, "\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't on everyone's mind the way it was a few weeks ago," a Japanese bank trader said. \par \par \uc2  Japanese exporters refrained from aggressive dollar sales Monday, perhaps on expectations that the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could retake the Y120 level ahead of this Friday's U.S. holiday. \par \par \uc2  But exporters were said to be selling euros for yen to lock in profits, the bank trader added. The euro managed to break above Y137.20 resistance at one point, but fell back below Y137 on exporter sales. \par \par \uc2  Against the dollar, the euro managed to recover solidly above $1.1400, after dipping below that late last Friday, but once again, the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to clear $1.1450 in Asian time. \par \par \uc2  -By Lisa Twaronite, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; lisa.twaronite@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  -Edited by Hugh Lawson \par \par \uc2  The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly. \par \par \uc2  Subscribers can find this table: \par \par \uc2  -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087. \par \par \uc2  -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX \par \par \uc2  -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT \par \par \uc2  -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030630dz6u000ec\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
