\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar entrenched ahead of Fed, BoJ talk flares up. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Justyna Pawlak \par \uc2 610 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juni 2003\par 12:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 25 (Reuters) - The dollar drifted in a tight range near recent five-week highs on the euro on Wednesday as investors nervously awaited a U.S. interest rate move, but it pared losses on the yen on wariness of yen selling by Japan. \par \par \uc2  Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment on whether the monetary authorities had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market after the dollar rose about half a yen in a matter of minutes in the European session, sparking talk of official involvement. \par \par \uc2  The market's preoccupation with the outcome of the Federal Reserve's highly uncertain decision meant that an uptick in Germany's Ifo business sentiment index gave little fresh fuel to the euro aside from a brief, initial uptick on the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "There is an unusual sense of disorientation in the market," said Aziz McMahon, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN Amro. \par \par \uc2  "A large number of macroeconomic forces are being digested... and the market wants some clarity. \par \par \uc2  "There was talk of BoJ (Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but the market focus is on the Fed," he said. \par \par \uc2  By 0943 GMT, the dollar was slightly lower against the euro at $1.1521, pulling away from recent five-week highs on the retreating single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the dollar was down 0.17 percent from the previous session's close at 117.66, after a sudden jump from below 117.40 to about 117.80 earlier. \par \par \uc2  "We see a couple of Japanese names buying (dollar/yen) and a (U.S. investment bank) out of Tokyo. The BoJ is trying to stem the tide," a European bank trader in London said when the yen was falling. \par \par \uc2  Throughout the Asian session, the yen was rising on the dollar due to demand from Japanese exporters trying to meet end-month obligations, until it suddenly reversed course. \par \par \uc2  Japanese monetary authorities have gone into the market covertly to limit the yen's rise against the struggling dollar over the past few months in a bid to protect the competitiveness of the export-dependent economy. \par \par \uc2  MODEST OR AGGRESSIVE? \par \par \uc2  Not only are expectations split whether the Federal Reserve will ease by 25 or 50 basis points when it announces its rate decision at 1815 GMT but implications for the dollar are also unclear. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts expect the greenback to draw support from a growth-boosting cut while others see it falling on a greater yield disadvantage. \par \par \uc2  "Expectations are evenly divided. Assuming a 50 basis points cut is bad and 25 is good for the dollar seems overly simplistic because what's going to come out of the statement will be more important," said Steven Pearson, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Halifax Bank of Scotland Treasury Services in London. \par \par \uc2  The German Ifo institute's closely-watched business climate index rose to 88.8 in June from May's 87.6, beating analysts' expectations. \par \par \uc2  There had been last-minute market jitters that the index would fall following a plunge in the June Belgium business confidence index to its lowest level since January 1993. \par \par \uc2  Norway, which still has one of the highest short-term rates in developed economies, has its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  executive board meeting today and is expected to cut rates by 100 basis points from the current rate of five percent at 1200 GMT. \par \par \uc2  The crown hit a two-month low against the dollar at 7.1300 on Wednesday and was trading just above two-year lows on the euro set earlier this month. \par \par \uc2  Earlier in the day the BoJ, after concluding a one-day meeting, said it would keep its current monetary policy unchanged. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030625dz6p00k2a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
