\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr Slips Vs Yen In Quiet Trade Ahead Of FOMC \b0\par\par\uc2  By Jonathan Soble \par \uc2 717 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juni 2003\par 07:54\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The dollar slipped against the yen in subdued Asian trading Wednesday ahead of the U.S. Federal Reserve's long-awaited interest rate decision later in the day. \par \par \uc2  The greenback's slightly weaker tone came as market players trimmed short positions on the yen against a raft of other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the euro and Australian and Canadian dollars. \par \par \uc2  "With the market focused on interest rate gaps for the last month or so, a lot of yen-shorts have built up," said Masamichi Koike, chief spot dealer at Sumitomo-Mitsui Bank. \par \par \uc2  "People are adjusting their positions, but it's too early to call it a trend" toward a broadly stronger yen. \par \par \uc2  Japan's near-zero short-term interest rates make the yen a net loser when investors are chasing the highest yields. \par \par \uc2  In a widely-expected decision, Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decided Wednesday to keep its monetary policy steady. The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market wasn't ruffled. \par \par \uc2  It was the first time since Governor Toshihiko Fukui took his position on March 20 that the Bank of Japan ended a policy meeting without altering monetary or other policy settings. \par \par \uc2  BOJ watchers said recent rises in Japanese share prices and a more stable bond market this week - following a selloff of government bonds last Thursday - took pressure off the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The market's focus remained on the U.S. Fed. \par \par \uc2  Opinion remained split on whether the Fed will opt for a 25 or 50 basis-point rate cut, but many traders said the real question is whether, as expected, it maintains a bias toward further easing. \par \par \uc2  "If it does, then apart from some knee-jerk selling (of the dollar) the reaction could be pretty muted," said Shuji Takano, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Aozora Bank. \par \par \uc2  "After all, in the big picture there's not a whole lot of difference between 25 and 50 basis points." \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y117.50, below Y117.89 late Tuesday in New York. The dollar was at Y117.90 late Tuesday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.1510, unchanged from late Tuesday in New York. The euro was at $1.1555 in Tokyo Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y135.28, down from Y135.69 in New York late Tuesday. The euro was at Y136.21 in Tokyo late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's slide against the yen was mitigated by the specter of yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "A lot of people think the Finance Ministry has an initial line of defense in the mid-Y117's," Aozora's Takano said. \par \par \uc2  Dollar bears were reluctant to push far below that line, keeping the U.S. unit's losses to a minimum. The dollar's intraday low was Y117.46. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian and Australian dollars both slipped against the yen Wednesday. The Canadian dollar was down around Y0.25 at Y86.48, while the Aussie unit fell about Y0.20 to around Y78.00. \par \par \uc2  Also Wednesday, Japan's trade and industry minister kept up pressure on China to scrap the yuan's peg to the dollar. China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy gained attention last week when U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow suggested Beijing might be close to revaluating the yuan, which is pegged at around CNY8.28 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Takeo Hiranuma told a parliamentary committee that consensus is growing in the international community that China should revaluate its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , given China's strong economy and its membership in the World Trade Organization. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate of a country should reflect the fundamentals of that country," Hiranuma said. \par \par \uc2  Japan for some time has accused China of "exporting deflation" with an overly weak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  -By Jonathan Soble, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; jonathan.soble@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  -Edited by Alastair Gale \par \par \uc2  The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly. \par \par \uc2  Subscribers can find this table: \par \par \uc2  -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087. \par \par \uc2  -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX \par \par \uc2  -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT \par \par \uc2  -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030625dz6p000bc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
