\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar stable,drip-fed US data builds Fed diagnosis. \b0\par\par\uc2 539 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juni 2003\par 10:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  By Charlotte Cooper LONDON, June 17 (Reuters) - The dollar held steady one cent off recent record lows against the euro on Tuesday as mixed signals from the U.S. economy increased uncertainties about the magnitude of the Federal Reserve's expected rate cut next week. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, a strong reading for a regional U.S. manufacturing report helped soothe worries about the economy, sending U.S. blue-chip stocks to the highest level in almost a year. \par \par \uc2  Consumer prices and other data for May are due out of the United States later in the session but analysts said they may not help in ascertaining the size of a Fed rate cut. \par \par \uc2  "Key indicators on inflation, industrial production and the housing market will give us a further insight whether the Fed will move by a more aggressive 50 basis points," said Paul Robson, international economist at Bank One. \par \par \uc2  "But it's unlikely that the numbers will give us a sure idea about what decision the Fed will make." \par \par \uc2  By 0730 GMT, the euro was quoted at $1.1830 from Monday's late New York level of $1.1825, after retesting last month's record high above $1.1930 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar couldn't find a clear direction against the yen, while wariness over possible Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to lend support, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  It was quoted steady on the day at 117.62 yen, holding within a tight range in Asian and European trade. \par \par \uc2  The euro was steady at 139.30 yen. \par \par \uc2  EURO ZONE SEEN STAGNANT \par \par \uc2  Before the U.S. data, Germany's ZEW institute releases its economic sentiment index, viewed as a useful precursor to the IFO business sentiment survey due later in the month. \par \par \uc2  The ZEW index is forecast at 19.2 in June conpared with 18.7 in May. \par \par \uc2  "We expect the number to be broadly static on the month, consistent with the idea that the euroland economy isn't going anywhere quickly," Robson said. \par \par \uc2  European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Wim Duisenberg told bankers at a dinner in Frankfurt on Monday night that the outlook for price stability was good. His comments followed remarks by ECB council members Ernst Welteke and Matti Vanhala that politicians must help boost growth now by pushing through economic reforms. \par \par \uc2  U.S. CPI is due at 1230 GMT along with May housing starts. \par \par \uc2  Economists polled by Reuters say the index is likely to have slipped 0.1 percent in May after declining 0.3 percent in April. Excluding volatile foods and energy, consumer prices are projected to rise 0.1 percent after remaining steady in April. \par \par \uc2  "The basic vulnerability of the dollar still remains as the market seems keen to sell by factoring in poor economic indicators and a possible interest rate cut," said Takashi Toyahara, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  section manager at Nomura Securities in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  In \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , monetary authorities are thought to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  several times since early June, but top financial diplomat, Zembei Mizoguchi, said on Tuesday that he could not comment on such speculation. \par \par \uc2  Toyahara said ther market was steering clear of trading dollar/yen as a result. \par \par \uc2  "Caution over \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is clearly sapping energy from the dollar/yen market," he said. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030617dz6h00e1s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
