\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro recovers, market eyes euro zone, U.S. easing. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 579 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 2003\par 09:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 11 (Reuters) - The euro on Wednesday recovered losses made in the previous session after European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Wim Duisenberg warned of further euro zone rate cuts, as markets also looked to further U.S. easing. \par \par \uc2  Duisenberg said in two newspaper interviews on Tuesday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had room to manoeuvre on interest rates, adding that a strong euro was unfavourable for exports to the United States. \par \par \uc2  But Fed Governor Donald Kohn also said on Tuesday that the Federal Reserve had tools to spur economic growth even if it runs out of room to cut interest rates, bolstering market expectations of a rate cut. \par \par \uc2  "It seem the ECB is happy to cut rates again, but Duisenberg's comments come so soon after last week's rate cut that the market is taking a 'wait and see' attitude," said Mark Henry, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at GNI. \par \par \uc2  "We have a light economic calendar this week, and the euro is likely to remain in a $1.15 to $1.20 range." \par \par \uc2  The euro rose a quarter percent from the U.S. close to $1.17  by 0720 GMT, more than two cents below record highs set last month and in the middle of recent ranges. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said options barriers at $1.19 and $1.1650 were restricting the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's movements. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was steady against the yen at 117.80 , again in the middle of recent ranges, while the euro was trading at 138 yen , above earlier three-week lows of 137.25. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was steady against the euro  after recouping on Tuesday some of the previous session's steep losses made on a UK Treasury study suggesting the pound needs to weaken substantially before joining the euro. \par \par \uc2  CUT REMOVES EURO SHINE \par \par \uc2  The ECB lowered its benchmark interest rate by half a percentage point to two percent last week, taking some shine off the euro which had enjoyed a recent rally to lifetime highs thanks to the interest rate differential with U.S. rates. \par \par \uc2  Bund futures hit contract highs on Wednesday in expectation of further euro zone rate cuts. \par \par \uc2  U.S. interest rates are currently at 1.25 percent, and further rate cuts are also widely expected. \par \par \uc2  The Fed's Beige Book summary of U.S. economic conditions is due at 1800 GMT, and Fed speakers Susan Schmidt Bies, Roger Ferguson and Robert McTeer are also due later, following dovish comments from Fed members on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  YEN WARINESS \par \par \uc2  Traders meanwhile remain reluctant to buy the yen on wariness of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , following significant sales of yen by Japanese monetary authorities in recent months. \par \par \uc2  "There are worries of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the downside but even with that aside, dollar/yen is not moving these days," said Takashi Toyahara, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  section manager at Nomura Securities in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  "The market is clearly taking a wait-and-see stance." \par \par \uc2  Japanese gross domestic product for the January-March quarter grew 0.1 percent, better than the preliminary zero change it announced last month. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan said it was keeping monetary policy unchanged and also said it would buy up to one trillion yen in asset-backed securities with credit ratings as low as BB - a move aimed at helping small firms having difficulties borrowing from Japan's struggling banks. \par \par \uc2  Japanese government bond yields, meanwhile, hit record lows on concern about the prospect of prolonged deflation in Japan. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030611dz6b00g22\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
