\par\par \b \uc2  BC-MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2). \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mariko Hayashibara \par \uc2 615 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 2003\par 08:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 11 (Reuters) - The yen rose on Wednesday due to a mixture of factors including demand from foreigners buying Japanese stocks and from domestic firms preparing to transfer assets to state pension funds. Major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded in razor-thin ranges, but the euro edged lower against the yen towards its three-week low of around 137 yen. \par \par \uc2  "Besides demand from exporters, the yen's recent appreciation has been driven by foreign investors' growing appetite for Japanese stocks and yen demand from domestic investors transferring pension assets to the government," said Tomoko Fujii, economic and market analysis director at Nikko Citigroup. \par \par \uc2  Finance Ministry data released on Wednesday showed that foreigners' net buying of Japanese stocks rose to 840.2 billion yen ($7.14 billion) in May from 347.2 billion yen in April. \par \par \uc2  It was the highest figure since May 2002 when foreigner buying totalled 931.7 billion yen. \par \par \uc2  "Foreign investors have not necessarily become optimistic about Japan, it's just a reflection of the global recovery in stock prices. But the (stock) buying has been supporting the yen," Fujii said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 117.89/94 yen , down from the day's high of 118.14 yen and near the late New York level of 117.74/78 yen. \par \par \uc2  The greenback dipped to a low of 117.64 yen, but the yen's movement in either direction was limited because traders were reluctant to buy the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on fears of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and saw no compelling reason to sell it. \par \par \uc2  "There are worries of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the downside but even with that aside, dollar/yen is not moving these days," said Takashi Toyahara, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  section manager at Nomura Securities. \par \par \uc2  "The market is clearly taking a wait-and-see stance." \par \par \uc2  Amid that atmosphere a surprise upward revision in Japan's growth data and the Bank of Japan's latest policy decision had little affect on the yen. \par \par \uc2  The government said gross domestic product for the January-March quarter grew 0.1 percent, better than the preliminary 0.0 percent change it announced last month. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan stepped up its efforts to alleviate funding problems at small businesses on Wednesday, promising to buy debt securities including those considered below investment grade. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which also announced it was keeping monetary policy unchanged, said it would buy up to one trillion yen ($8.49 billion) in asset-backed securities with credit ratings as low as BB - a move aimed at helping small firms having difficulties borrowing from Japan's struggling banks. \par \par \uc2  EURO PRESSURED \par \par \uc2  The euro stayed under pressure against the dollar and yen as dealers bet on more rate cuts by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) following hints from its president, Wim Duisenberg. \par \par \uc2  Duisenberg said in two newspaper interviews that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had room to manoeuvre on interest rates, adding that a strong euro was unfavourable for exports to the United States. \par \par \uc2  The ECB lowered its benchmark interest rate by half a percentage point to two percent last week, taking some shine off the euro which had enjoyed a rally to lifetime highs thanks to the interest rate differential with U.S. rates. \par \par \uc2  Prospects of a rate cut, which caused profit-taking sales in the euro, and the yen's broad demand pushed the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down as low as 137.22 yen from the day's high of 138.26 yen  before coming back to 138.03/18 yen. \par \par \uc2  Against the dollar, the euro recovered to $1.1710/15  from $1.1668/74 in late U.S. trading, but the upside was still fragile, dealers said. ($1=117.73 yen). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030611dz6b00dmq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
