\par\par \b \uc2  Euro creeps lower as market eyes more ECB rate cuts. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Yonggi Kang \par \uc2 568 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 2003\par 04:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 11 (Reuters) - The euro stayed under pressure against the dollar and yen on Wednesday as dealers bet on more rate cuts by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  following hints from its president, Wim Duisenberg. Major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were trading in razor-thin ranges in morning trade but the euro was edging lower against the yen towards its three-week low of around 137 yen. \par \par \uc2  "The market is selling the euro on expectations of more ECB monetary easing," said a dealer at a Japanese trust bank. \par \par \uc2  Duisenberg said in two newspaper interviews that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had room to manoeuvre on interest rates. \par \par \uc2  "Further rate cuts are possible because interest rates in the euro area are still higher than that in the United States," he was reported to have said on the sidelines of an Amsterdam event to launch his biography. \par \par \uc2  The ECB lowered its benchmark interest rate by half a percentage point to two percent last week, taking some shine off the euro which had enjoyed a rally to lifetime highs thanks to the interest rate differential with U.S. rates. The U.S. Fed funds rate is now at 1.25 percent. \par \par \uc2  At 0204 GMT, the euro was trading at 137.36/50 yen slightly lower than the New York close of 137.39/53 yen and down more than a full yen from Tokyo's opening level on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Against the dollar, the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was changing hands at $1.1672/77 against $1.1668/74 in late U.S. trading. \par \par \uc2  Traders peg $1.16 as the next crucial support. \par \par \uc2  DOLLAR LETHARGIC VS YEN \par \par \uc2  The dollar was moving sideways against the yen in lethargic trade, because traders were afraid to buy the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on fears of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and saw no compelling reason to sell it. \par \par \uc2  "There are worries of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the downside but even with that aside, dollar/yen is not moving these days. The market is clearly taking a wait-and-see stance," said Takashi Toyahara, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  section manager at Nomura Securities. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 117.73/78 yen almost unchanged from 117.74/78 yen in late New York. \par \par \uc2  Even a surprise upward revision in Japan's growth data failed to affect sentiment in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The government said gross domestic product for the January-March quarter grew 0.1 percent, better than the preliminary 0.0 percent change it announced last month. And a keenly awaited speech by U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow at the Japan Society in New York had no significant impact on the dollar as he made no mention of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan ends its two-day policy-setting meeting later in the day but dealers do not expect anything startling. \par \par \uc2  Earlier on Wednesday, Zembei Mizoguchi, Japan's top financial diplomat, said a further rise in the yen was unwarranted and that authorities would act if needed to correct excessive moves in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Separately, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would disclose the volume of its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a monthly basis starting this month. \par \par \uc2  The MOF currently discloses details of its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a quarterly basis, but the market can easily estimate the monthly volume from the Bank of Japan's money market data released at the end of the month. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030611dz6b004sa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
