\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 :Dlr, Euro Spike Vs Yen;  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Suspected \b0\par\par\uc2  By Jonathan Soble \par \uc2 447 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 2003\par 07:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The dollar regained lost ground against the yen in Asia Wednesday, but a midday spike that many traders said may be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities failed to ignite a sustained rally. \par \par \uc2  The dollar jumped about half a yen just before noon after moving sideways throughout the morning, making some traders suspect fresh yen-selling by Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Last month the MOF sold a record Y4 trillion through the Bank of Japan to curb the yen's rise against the dollar, and most traders believe Tokyo has poured more money into the market in June. \par \par \uc2  The government fears an excessively strong yen could hobble Japan's crucial export sector, which drove the country's economic rebound last year. \par \par \uc2  There was no way to confirm whether the MOF ordered \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday, as the ministry only acknowledges selling yen days or weeks after the fact. \par \par \uc2  But "price action suggests they've been selling," said the head trader at a Tokyo-based foreign brokerage. \par \par \uc2  "It's a very, very artificial market," he said. \par \par \uc2  However, the impact of any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was modest and short-lived. \par \par \uc2  After hitting an intraday high of Y118.10, the dollar faded in the latter half of the session - a sign, traders said, that the market isn't ready to get behind a sustained rebound in the greenback. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar won't break upwards unless there's real evidence that the U.S. economy is improving," said Mitsubishi Securities' Minoru Shioiri. \par \par \uc2  The euro also gained on the Japanese unit Wednesday, rebounding above Y138 after plunging more than a yen and a half to around Y137.20 overnight. \par \par \uc2  Some traders said the MOF may also have ordered the BOJ to sell yen for euros to prevent the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from losing more ground. \par \par \uc2  The euro's upward momentum against the yen spread to the euro-dollar, erasing some of the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's overnight losses and bringing it back above $1.1700. \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y117.89, above Y117.68 late Tuesday in New York. The dollar was at Y118.17 late Tuesday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.1705, higher than $1.1677 late Tuesday in New York. The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at $1.1725 in Tokyo Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y138.02, up from Y137.41 in New York late Tuesday. The euro was at Y138.58 in Tokyo late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.6530, up from $1.6509 in New York and higher than $1.6492 in Tokyo Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030611dz6b000ar\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
