\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  MOF/ \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Data -2: To Coincide With BOJ Data \b0\par\par\uc2 251 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 2003\par 02:47\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- Starting at the end of June, Japan's finance ministry will announce on a monthly basis the amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  it conducted during the month, a ministry official said Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The data, which will only include the total amount of funds spent in yen, will be released on the last business day of each month, the official said. The ministry currently only releases \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  data on a quarterly basis. \par \par \uc2  The timing of the release will likely coincide with the Bank of Japan's data on monthly changes in its current account balance, which is also released at the end of the month, and which also roughly reveals the amount of funds spent on \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducts \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on directions from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The new MOF monthly data, like the BOJ data, will not include the last two business days of the month, for which settlements are made in the following month, the MOF official said. \par \par \uc2  Since the start of the year, the finance ministry has been conducting "covert" \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at weakening the yen, but has refrained from acknowledging the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  until after the BOJ data forced its hand. \par \par \uc2  Last month, the ministry admitted it spent around Y4 trillion, a record for a single month, to curb excessive strength in the yen. \par \par \uc2  -By Miyako Takebe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; miyako.takebe@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  -Edited by Kirsty Mackenzie \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030611dz6b0001u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
