\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -2: BOJ Ops Hint At  \highlight22\uc2 Japan FX Intervention \highlight\uc2  Fri \b0\par\par\uc2 394 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juni 2003\par 08:56\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Since \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  has abandoned its policy of overtly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  through the BOJ in favor of "stealth" bids placed through a few banks, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  players have become adept at searching for market clues that suggest whether or not the BOJ may have been active. \par \par \uc2  Talk that Japan may have once again acted to stem the yen's rise Friday was further fueled by unusual BOJ money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ's move to absorb Y1 trillion in funds by selling discount bills starting Tuesday may indicate that the bank sold a large amount of yen in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  surprised money market players, who hadn't expected such a large excess of funds for Tuesday, and led to speculation that the BOJ was acting to absorb yen sold Friday that will settle in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  In May, after dollar fell within a few ticks of Y115, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold nearly Y4 trillion in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a record for \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a single month. \par \par \uc2  Trust bank selling also weighed on the euro Monday, traders said. Against the yen, the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  came close to falling below options-related support at Y138.00 at one point, below which it hasn't traded since May 26. \par \par \uc2  Against the dollar, the euro continued to face profit-taking pressure from market participants who think the pair will correct before resuming its recent uptrend. While most medium-term forecasts still favor a stronger euro, market consensus is more divided in the short-term. \par \par \uc2  Last week, Goldman Sachs joined the short-term euro bull camp when it hiked its three-month euro/dollar forecast to $1.1800, and abandoned its view "that the euro/dollar will correct to $1.1200 within 3 months, before resuming its uptrend," strategist Jim O'Neill wrote in a research report. \par \par \uc2  -By Lisa Twaronite, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; lisa.twaronite@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  -Edited by Alastair Gale \par \par \uc2  The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly. \par \par \uc2  Subscribers can find this table: \par \par \uc2  -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087. \par \par \uc2  -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX \par \par \uc2  -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT \par \par \uc2  -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030609dz69000e0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
