\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 :Dlr Loses Ground To Yen, But MOF Talk Supports \b0\par\par\uc2  By Lisa Twaronite \par \uc2 654 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juni 2003\par 07:56\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The dollar bumped lower against the yen in Asia Monday, but remained supported by talk that the Japanese financial authorities propped the pair up late last week and would likely do so again. \par \par \uc2  After peaking early in the session at Y118.76 just ahead of 0000 GMT, the dollar began to drop as foreign funds bought yen for investment purposes, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Japanese trust banks were also said to be selling dollars in order to repatriate yen on behalf of Japanese companies preparing to hand back some of their pension funds to the government. \par \par \uc2  But support at Y118.30 held, as market participants were hesitant to test the downside on talk that the Bank of Japan sold yen in New York last Friday on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Overseas fund inflows and Japanese pension-related dollar selling "is likely to cap the range, with that on one side and the BOJ on the other side," said J.P. Morgan strategist James Malcolm. \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y118.33, below Y118.71 in New York Friday but above Y117.63 in Tokyo late Friday. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.1697, higher than $1.1689 in New York and $1.1848 in Tokyo Friday. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y138.41, compared with Y138.76 in New York and Y139.44 in Tokyo Friday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.6597, compared with $1.6620 in New York and $1.6624 in Tokyo Friday. \par \par \uc2  Since Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  has abandoned its policy of overtly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  through the BOJ in favor of "stealth" bids placed through a few banks, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  players have become adept at searching for market clues that suggest whether or not the BOJ may have been active. \par \par \uc2  Talk that Japan may have once again acted to stem the yen's rise Friday was further fueled by unusual BOJ money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ's move to absorb Y1 trillion in funds by selling discount bills starting Tuesday may indicate that the bank sold a large amount of yen in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  surprised money market players, who hadn't expected such a large excess of funds for Tuesday, and led to speculation that the BOJ was acting to absorb yen sold Friday that will settle in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  In May, after dollar fell within a few ticks of Y115, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold nearly Y4 trillion in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a record for \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a single month. \par \par \uc2  Trust bank selling also weighed on the euro Monday, traders said. Against the yen, the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  came close to falling below options-related support at Y138.00 at one point, below which it hasn't traded since May 26. \par \par \uc2  Against the dollar, the euro continued to face profit-taking pressure from market participants who think the pair will correct before resuming its recent uptrend. While most medium-term forecasts still favor a stronger euro, market consensus is more divided in the short-term. \par \par \uc2  Last week, Goldman Sachs joined the short-term euro bull camp when it hiked its three-month euro/dollar forecast to $1.1800, and abandoned its view "that the euro/dollar will correct to $1.1200 within 3 months, before resuming its uptrend," strategist Jim O'Neill wrote in a research report. \par \par \uc2  -By Lisa Twaronite, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; lisa.twaronite@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  -Edited by Alastair Gale \par \par \uc2  The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly. \par \par \uc2  Subscribers can find this table: \par \par \uc2  -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087. \par \par \uc2  -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX \par \par \uc2  -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT \par \par \uc2  -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030609dz69000bb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
