\par\par \b \uc2  Euro buoyant - eyes peeled for  \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mariko Hayashibara \par \uc2 584 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juni 2003\par 04:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 6 (Reuters) - The euro kept its strength on Friday after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) cut interest rates by 50 basis points and as pessimism reappeared about the dollar following disappointing U.S. data. \par \par \uc2  Japanese officials were busy talking down the yen against the dollar, which fell as low as around 117.30 yen in post-Asian trade on Thursday, leaving market participants wary about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Caution over \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was already seen with the dollar above 118 yen, so the mood is to go long on the dollar as \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is widely expected," said Junya Tanase, global markets officer at J.P. Morgan Chase. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa reiterated on Friday that Japan would take action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if necessary, but the government did not intend to artificially manipulate \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates. \par \par \uc2  Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi echoed that sentiment, saying he wants stability in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and would take necessary measures to keep it. \par \par \uc2  At 0149 GMT, the dollar was quoted at 117.85/90 yen up from the late New York level of 117.62/70 yen. \par \par \uc2  But disappointing data from the United States, in tandem with the ECB' rate cut, helped to boost the euro against the greenback. \par \par \uc2  The number of people applying for U.S. jobless aid rose to its highest level in more than a month, while April factory orders sank 2.9 percent, the largest drop in 17 months. \par \par \uc2  The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading at $1.1853/58 slightly up from the late New York level of $1.1841/47. It rose as high as $1.1890 following the ECB's decision. \par \par \uc2  Against the Japanese unit, the euro rose to 139.66/78 yen from the late U.S. level of 139.38 yen. The post-ECB high was around 139.80 yen. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said investors were bargain-hunting the euro for the yen after steep falls the previous day to 137.72 yen, and this was indirectly supporting the dollar/yen. \par \par \uc2  EURO TO LOSE SHINE? \par \par \uc2  Underlying sentiment for the euro remained bullish, but dealers and analysts said the single unit was unlikely to return in the near term to its record level of $1.1935 hit in late May. \par \par \uc2  "The market priced in a rate cut of 50 basis points, so the euro's jump was a classic buyback after selling on speculation," said Koji Fukaya, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi. \par \par \uc2  "From a standpoint of interest rate differential, I don't think the euro will keep rising. I expect it to gradually lose its shine." \par \par \uc2  Following the ECB's aggressive rate cut, all eyes are on what the Federal Reserve will do later this month. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said that although the ECB's cut narrowed the euro-zone's interest rate differential with the United States, signs of weakness in U.S. economic data are boosting investors' expectations that the Fed will also cut interest rates. \par \par \uc2  "We'll be eagerly waiting to see today's U.S. jobs data for a clue about what the Fed will do," said a Japanese trust bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  The Labor Department's report on non-farm payrolls is due at 1230 GMT. \par \par \uc2  A Reuters poll showed a consensus forecast that 39,000 jobs were lost in May, compared with a loss of 48,000 in April. The jobless rate, however, was expected to rise to 6.1 percent from 6.0 percent. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030606dz66004sb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
