\par\par \b \uc2  Euro broadly sold as dealers eye hefty ECB rate cut. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Yonggi Kang \par \uc2 522 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juni 2003\par 04:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 5 (Reuters) - Expectations of a hefty rate cut by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  prompted dealers to dump the euro against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday, working as a drag on the dollar against the yen as well. \par \par \uc2  The once high-flying euro extended losses to break the 138 yen mark, hitting a two-week low of 137.72 yen as offshore players rushed to buy the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the run-up to the ECB's rate-setting meeting later in the day. \par \par \uc2  The fall in euro/yen also put pressure on the euro against the dollar, prompting the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to move closer to crucial support at $1.16. \par \par \uc2  "We've been seeing such euro-selling every day but it seems like U.S. investment banks are selling the euro now," said Kosuke Hanao, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Royal Bank of Scotland in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Dealers have been squaring positions ahead of the rate verdict as the majority of players are betting on a 50-basis point cut from the current benchmark rate of 2.50 percent. \par \par \uc2  "The market has pretty much factored in a 50 basis-point cut," Hanao said. \par \par \uc2  A rate reduction will take some shine off the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , because interest rate differentials between the euro zone and the United States will narrow. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. fed funds rate is now at 1.25 percent. \par \par \uc2  ECB President Wim Duisenberg and Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan both hinted at lower interest rates from their respective banks in remarks made on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The ECB rate announcement is due at 1145 GMT. \par \par \uc2  DEALERS EYE MORE CUTS \par \par \uc2  Traders say further ECB rate cuts may be down the road. \par \par \uc2  "Even if the ECB cuts rates by 50 basis points, I think they'll still have a feeling that they haven't completely emptied their bladder yet," said a dealer at Mizuho Corporate Bank. \par \par \uc2  At 0228 GMT, the euro was trading at 137.84/96 yen compared with 138.32/48 yen in late New York. \par \par \uc2  Against the dollar, the euro was quoted at $1.1638/43 versus the U.S. close at $1.1639/45. \par \par \uc2  Trading in dollar/yen was mostly driven by moves in the euro as the market lacked other factors to trade on. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's downside is firmly supported by fears of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with some dealers saying that the Japanese authorities were probably \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Hiroshi Watanabe, head of the Finance Ministry's international bureau, said on Wednesday that the ministry would stay vigilant against speculative \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market movements that pushed the yen higher. \par \par \uc2  Japan conducted the largest ever monthly volume of yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in May, totalling some four trillion yen ($33.66 billion), to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise. \par \par \uc2  Separately, Bank of Japan Policy Board member Toshikatsu Fukuma said on Thursday that a weaker dollar would pose uncertainties on the domestic and overseas economies. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted at 118.44/49 yen compared with 118.81/89 yen in late New York trading. ($1=118.83 Yen). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030605dz65005eq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
