\par\par \b \uc2  Kuroda lends support for dollar but upside capped. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Yonggi Kang \par \uc2 609 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juni 2003\par 04:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 4 (Reuters) - The dollar kept its firm tone against the yen on Wednesday on comments by Japan's former top financial diplomat touting a weaker yen, but the greenback's upside was capped by exporter selling offers. \par \par \uc2  Haruhiko Kuroda, former vice finance minister for international affairs and now an adviser to Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi, said in an interview on Japanese television late on Tuesday that a dollar/yen rate of 140 yen would be appropriate from a standpoint of purchasing power parity (PPP). \par \par \uc2  PPP is a way to compare living costs between nations by looking at prices of similar items. The gauge to calculate it can be anything from a hamburger to the consumer price index. \par \par \uc2  Analysts have said the appropriate exchange rate using PPP could vary greatly - within a range of 70 yen to 165 yen - depending on what kind of benchmark is used. \par \par \uc2  "Kuroda's comments was one factor behind the dollar's gains," said a dealer at a major Japanese bank. \par \par \uc2  "Whether the comments will affect the market in the longer term is another question." \par \par \uc2  Many dealers do not expect the remarks to have a lasting impact on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates because a 140 yen level was considered unrealistic at present and similar comments by Kuroda's former boss, Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa, have had no material impact on the market. \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa has said that he preferred the dollar/yen rate moving closer to 150-160 yen based on PPP. \par \par \uc2  Remarks by Koizumi earlier on Tuesday that the yen was overvalued relative to Japan's economy also provided a boost for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At 0120 GMT, the dollar was quoted at 119.21/26 yen compared with 119.14/22 yen in late New York. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect the dollar to remain trapped in a 118-120 yen range for now because the downside is firmly supported by fears of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while the upside is capped by offers from Japanese exporter companies. \par \par \uc2  "I think it's going to be hard for dollar/yen to break beyond the current range because there's quite a lot of dollar selling orders from exporters," said Hiroyuki Watanabe, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Shinsei Bank. \par \par \uc2  MARKET EYEING ECB \par \par \uc2  The dollar was also on solid ground against the euro, although trading was more cautious ahead of a European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate-setting meeting on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Many in the market expect a cut in the current benchmark refinancing rate - currently at 2.50 percent - as European policymakers have hinted at prospects of monetary easing. \par \par \uc2  ECB President Wim Duisenberg told a banking conference in Berlin on Tuesday that inflation pressures "have declined significantly over recent months," and could possibly fall below the euro zone's two percent ceiling in 2004, allowing the bank room to cut rates to spur borrowing and investment. \par \par \uc2  "If they do lower rates, they'll probably do it at 50 basis points," said another Japanese bank dealer. "I think the ECB has a tendency to make big moves at once as opposed to the Fed which tweaks policy bit by bit." \par \par \uc2  Shinsei's Watanabe expected a rate cut of 25 basis points. \par \par \uc2  "There still are views in the market that they will not cut rates. On whether it's going to be 25 or 50, I think it's going to be 25," he said. \par \par \uc2  The euro was trading at $1.1731/36 against $1.1728/34 in late U.S. trading. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was quoted at 139.74/86 yen compared with 139.78/92 yen. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030604dz64004mq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
