\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Market yawns after Bush trumpets strong dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Yonggi Kang \par \uc2 602 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juni 2003\par 04:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 3 (Reuters) - The dollar edged lower against the yen on Tuesday in a market unimpressed by President George W. Bush's signal that he supported a strong U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar began the day's trade near late U.S. levels of 118.60 yen but gradually lost ground as U.S. funds sold the euro against the yen, acting as a drag on the greenback. \par \par \uc2  Late on Monday, a senior U.S. official said Bush told other Group of Eight leaders at their summit in the French spa resort of Evian that he favoured a strong dollar and that U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy was unchanged. \par \par \uc2  But the comment was seen providing little incentive to Tokyo dealers to push up the greenback. \par \par \uc2  "The market is reacting little to Bush's comments," said a dealer at a major Japanese bank. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market had factored in prospects of a discussion on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates at the summit after some leaders had shown concern about the dollar's fall and hinted the topic would be on the agenda. \par \par \uc2  The dollar has slid more than 10 percent to all-time lows against the euro this year. Against the yen it is in line with its rate at the start of the year after falling to 115.10 yen in mid-May. \par \par \uc2  At 0206 GMT, the dollar was trading at 118.45/50 yen compared with 118.62/70 in late New York. \par \par \uc2  Trading in the euro was lacklustre as caution ahead of a closely watched policy meeting by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday weighed on sentiment. \par \par \uc2  The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at $1.1726/32 against $1.1756/62 in late U.S. trading. \par \par \uc2  The euro dropped to 138.97/14 yen from late New York levels at 139.33/47 yen. \par \par \uc2  DEALERS QUESTION DOLLAR POLICY \par \par \uc2  Few dealers took Bush's comments at face value and many say the U.S. administration will probably take a non-\b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist\b0 \highlight\uc2 , laissez-faire approach to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates. \par \par \uc2  "Bush expressed his intention to maintain the strong dollar policy at the Evian summit but the market is showing doubt," said Kazuhiro Miyake, a strategist at Daiwa Institute of Research. \par \par \uc2  "A rapid fall in the dollar will be a negative factor for the U.S. economy but there's an underlying view that a gradual weakening of the dollar is in fact positive," he added. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese bank dealer concurred. \par \par \uc2  "What he really means with his 'strong dollar' policy is that the government will let the market decide \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates. If U.S. economic fundamentals are strong the dollar will strengthen, and if they're weak the dollar will weaken." \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa gave a nod to Bush's comments, saying at a news conference that Washington's "strong dollar" policy was appropriate. \par \par \uc2  With so many trades being done in dollars it would be a problem if the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  were not strong, Shiokawa said. \par \par \uc2  He did not elaborate. \par \par \uc2  Traders expect the dollar to have a hard time trying to break out of its trading range against the yen as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pair is caught between fears of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the downside and exporters' selling on the upside. \par \par \uc2  For the European single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the market is focused on Thursday's ECB meeting and Friday's U.S. jobs data for May. \par \par \uc2  Dealers are still split between a 25 basis point cut and a 50 basis point cut from the ECB's current benchmark refinancing rate at 2.50 percent. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030603dz63004sd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
