\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar builds on previous gains, yen recoils. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Justyna Pawlak \par \uc2 651 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Mai 2003\par 12:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, May 29 (Reuters) - The dollar touched a four-week high against the yen and added fresh gains to the previous session's sharp rise against the euro on Thursday as the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued its pause after a rapid rally. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said recent dollar selling had become overstretched and the greenback's snap back from this week's record low on the euro did not mean it had pulled out of its longer-term decline backed by weak economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  By 0950 GMT the dollar had peaked at $1.1692 per euro , gaining half a percent from the New York close almost two and a half cents above its lowest level since the euro's birth set on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "There is more scope for (euro) lows below $1.17 still," said Bilal Hafeez, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Deustche Bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "But over a few weeks or so the dollar-weakening trend will return. One of the main reasons is that the market is still too optimistic about U.S. growth," he said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's rise after weeks of spiralling downwards brought investor attention to the yen, which has seen frequent signs of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb its strength to safeguard the fragile economy. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par After a sharp bout of selling, the yen bottomed out at a fresh record\par low versus the euro of 139.88  and a four-week low on the dollar of\par 119.15       . It pulled back from these levels slightly in the\par European mid-session.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The underlying picture for the dollar has not changed much. All the\par market's telling you is that we have moved too far, too fast and there\par is room to pause and take stock," said Jim McCormick, head of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par research at Lehman Brothers.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "In that context dollar/yen has become a major focus. We've had a slew\par of modestly bad data out of Japan this week and the Bank of Japan is\par getting a lot of help in getting dollar/yen back to a level it feels\par comfortable with."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par RIDING A WAVE\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The greenback has gained strength against the yen due to concerns the\par Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to sell yen on behalf of the Finance\par Ministry.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Some dealers suspect the authorities, concerned yen strength will\par dampen exports, stepped in as recently as Tuesday, when the dollar fell\par to around 116.20 yen in post-Asian trade.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is believed to have \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  heavily in the past two weeks, and\par this was thought to be stopping the dollar from falling below 115 yen,\par dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I think a dollar-buying mood spread in the market once it rose beyond\par 118 yen," said Gen Kawabe, manager of the treasury department at Chuo\par Mitsui Trust and Banking.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, traders said Japanese exporters then took advantage of the\par higher levels to sell dollars for yen, which took the shine off the\par greenback.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par For the euro, the market's focus was shifting to next Thursday's\par European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  meeting to see if the ECB will cut interest rates\par from 2.5 percent currently.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the United States, San Francisco Federal Reserve President Robert\par Parry, a voting member on the Fed's policy making committee, said late\par on Wednesday the economy was still stuck in a soft patch.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He said the Fed still had room to cut rates in spite of forecasts of\par stronger growth because the pace of growth would not be fast enough to\par use up spare capacity in the economy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. data due at 1230 GMT includes weekly jobless claims which are\par expected to have fallen to 419,000 in the week ended May 24, from\par 428,000 a week earlier.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Commerce Department's second estimate of first-quarter growth is\par forecast to show the economy expanded 1.9 percent in the period.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030529dz5t00k86\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
