\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 :Dlr Up Vs Yen On Adjustments, Yen-Bearish Talk \b0\par\par\uc2  By Miyako Takebe \par \uc2 734 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Mai 2003\par 07:47\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The dollar leapt to its highest level in almost four weeks in Tokyo Thursday as foreign funds unwound speculative short dollar positions in the face of growing yen-negative sentiment. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  briefly broke above Y119 for the first time since May 5, before selling by Japanese exporters dragged it back down to the upper Y118s. \par \par \uc2  "Rumors that two major Japanese banking groups are in trouble and are facing nationalization likely helped shift sentiment among foreigners and led them to buy dollars," said Kaneo Ogino, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at HSBC in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Market views were mixed as to the origin of the unconfirmed rumors, with some citing a report by international consulting firm Medley Global Advisers, while others referred to a report by another consulting firm, Johnson Smick. \par \par \uc2  But many Tokyo traders noted the rumors likely accelerated dollar buying which had already begun as players unwound short dollar positions amid the euro's correction off an all-time high of 1.1935 hit earlier in the week. \par \par \uc2  "The stock market's calm reaction to talk of the consulting firm report...shows that it isn't really that big a concern," said Satoshi Tate, vice president for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at UFJ Bank. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar was unable to sustain its gains above Y119, as Japanese exporters were quick to act on the rise. \par \par \uc2  "Exporter offers have been constant after the break of Y119," said HSBC's Ogino, although he added there may be another test of that level later in the global session. \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y118.73, off its session high of Y119.17, but still slightly above Y118.65 late Wednesday in New York. The dollar was at Y117.10 late Wednesday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.1764, little changed from $1.1765 late Wednesday in New York. The euro was at $1.1840 in Tokyo Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y139.67, up from Y139.59 in New York late Wednesday. The euro was at Y138.65 in Tokyo late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.6375, up from $1.6370 in New York but lower than $1.6430 in Tokyo Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Some market players also mentioned the possibility that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's finance ministry, via the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , quietly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again overnight and on Thursday to help the dollar advance. The government is widely believed to have been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly this month to help support the dollar and to keep the yen from rising too far. \par \par \uc2  Although ministry officials have neither confirmed or denied the speculation, market players will be watching Friday's release of BOJ data on the sources of change in its monthly current account, which will effectively confirm the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by revealing the amount of money the government has spent in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market this month. \par \par \uc2  Even though the dollar advanced Thursday, Tokyo traders speculate the finance ministry will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  indefinitely, to prevent the yen from rising, if the dollar shows signs of slipping again. \par \par \uc2  "Their aim is to discourage those who want to sell dollars by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  again and again and again," Ogino said. \par \par \uc2  UFJ's Tate added the recent unwinding of dollar shorts was due in part to speculators giving up on holding on to such positions in the face of such strong government resolve to cap the yen. \par \par \uc2  The euro remained subdued against the dollar, continuing its correction from recent gains. \par \par \uc2  Some traders said selling to protect options barriers at $1.2000, as well as uncertainty ahead of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting on June 5, were keeping the euro from regaining lost ground. \par \par \uc2  Some are expecting the bank to cut interest rates by 0.25 percentage point, though others are looking at the possibility of 0.50 percentage point cut. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -By Miyako Takebe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929;\par miyako.takebe@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -Edited by Kirsty Mackenzie\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The chart of late Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates that accompanied Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has\par been replaced with an enhanced \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fixture that is updated\par hourly.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Subscribers can find this table:\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030529dz5t000bl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
