\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar rallies broadly as sentiment improves. \b0\par\par\uc2  By John Parry \par \uc2 703 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Mai 2003\par 22:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, May 28 (Reuters) - The dollar showed mettle on Wednesday in a broad-based rally that traders believe may have staying power, recovering from a symbolic blow when the euro hit record highs against the greenback in the prior session. \par \par \uc2  "Before, the euro had uncanny resilience, but since this morning there are some signs of capitulation," as a range of market participants including hedge funds and model-based investors took profits in the single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Grant Wilson, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with Mellon Bank in Pittsburgh, Penn. \par \par \uc2  Technical strategists said if the euro slips decisively below some key support areas, that could herald a move down to around $1.1550. Immediate support levels lie around $1.1707, then $1.1677, said Terence Gabriel, senior technical analyst with Bank of America in New York. \par \par \uc2  "The euro had reached severely extended levels and is vulnerable to a protracted downturn," Gabriel said. \par \par \uc2  An anticipated cut in euro zone interest rates when the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meets next week was one of the heaviest weights on the euro on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  ECB chief economist Otmar Issing reinforced the view cuts may come, saying the risk of deflation could not be ruled out in Germany, but that recent talk of a general decrease in prices was "less rational." \par \par \uc2  A cut to the euro zone's benchmark rates, currently 2.50 percent, would narrow the difference with U.S. benchmark rates of 1.25 percent and reduce the advantage euro-denominated deposits and investments hold over dollar-denominated assets. \par \par \uc2  Although the single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's retreat was the main catalyst for the dollar's rebound, partly as a result, the greenback strengthened broadly against the yen and other major rivals. Some traders cited talk of dollar buying from Japanese accounts just above the 118.0 yen area, amid persistent nervousness that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be prepared to undertake yen-weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Not even a weaker than expected April U.S. durable goods report on Tuesday - down 2.4 percent versus expectations for a decline of 1 percent - could halt the dollar's ascent. \par \par \uc2  "We are in the midst of a correction to the dollar's weakness and I wouldn't read too much into the durables number because we already know the manufacturing sector is weak and the report itself is very volatile," said Bob Lynch, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BNP Paribas in New York. \par \par \uc2  STOCKS HELP \par \par \uc2  Movements in other asset markets helped improve dollar sentiment, some analysts said. In particular, the ability of U.S. stocks to post modest gains in late afternoon trade on Wednesday, building on Tuesday's robust rally, helped burnish the greenback's allure. The possibility of a sustained equities rally could draw more foreign investors back to U.S. assets, check the widening of the U.S. current account deficit and help stabilize the dollar, said Wilson. \par \par \uc2  While the correlation between stock prices and the dollar appears to be back in force, the dollar's inverse price relationship with gold was also back in play, as gold prices slipped on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The euro fell to a session low of $1.1707. \par \par \uc2  By late afternoon on Wednesday in New York, the euro was at $1.1768, down 0.4 percent and down nearly 2 cents from its highest point in the prior session. On Tuesday the euro hit a record of $1.1932, the highest value since it was launched on Jan. 1, 1999. \par \par \uc2  But the euro rose briskly against the yen on Wednesday, in turn helping propel the greenback higher against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar traded as high as 118.92 yen, before slipping to 118.63 yen, still up 1.2 percent on the day. \par \par \uc2  The euro hit a record high 139.70 yen, The euro is trading in uncharted territory against the yen, making each session a potential high-water mark. \par \par \uc2  The dollar pulled up from Tuesday's 4-1/2-year low of 1.2779 Swiss francs to trade at 1.2941 francs, a gain of 0.6 percent but down from the session high of 1.3020 francs. \par \par \uc2  (Additional reporting by Daniel Bases). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030528dz5s013ih\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
