\par\par \b \uc2  Euro pauses to test support before next advance. \b0\par\par\uc2 436 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Mai 2003\par 01:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, May 28 (Reuters) - The euro took a breather in early Wednesday trade, a day after hitting a lifetime high against the dollar, with dealers expecting it to test support before heading upward to the next crucial target of $1.20. \par \par \uc2  "Moves were quite steep yesterday so the market is being hesitant to break above the closely watched $1.2 mark now," said Koichi Abe, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading manager at Aozora Bank. \par \par \uc2  On the back of demand for higher-yielding assets, the euro has risen 2.7 percent against the dollar in the last four sessions, hitting a record high in Tokyo on Tuesday and then extending gains to around $1.1935 in New York. \par \par \uc2  But dealers are cautious about the speed of the euro's rise, saying the market will not feel comfortable about pushing it higher until it finds solid support on the downside. \par \par \uc2  "We've heard many European policy-makers voicing their tolerance of a strong euro, but seeing it responding obediently to U.S. indicators, I think it's in a corrective mode now," said a dealer at a major Japanese securities firm. \par \par \uc2  Reports on Monday showed U.S. consumer confidence rose in May, though less than expected, while low mortgage rates spurred home buying in April. \par \par \uc2  At 2321 GMT the euro was quoted at $1.1815/19 versus $1.1812 in late New York. \par \par \uc2  Against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the euro was trading at 138.51/63 yen against the U.S. close of 138.48/59 yen. \par \par \uc2  One focus for the euro in the near term is the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy-setting meeting next week. \par \par \uc2  Some traders said the appeal of higher-yielding euro zone bonds may be waning as investors start to bet the ECB will cut interest rates at the meeting on June 5, which could start to weigh on the euro. \par \par \uc2  Others said market sentiment has become too slanted in favour of the euro, considering the euro zone's lacklustre economic performance. \par \par \uc2  Dealers do not expect the dollar to break beyond its well-worn trading range against the yen, especially after confirming that the upside is capped and with the downside supported by fears of yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The dollar is firming against the yen but I don't envisage it going beyond 120 yen," said the dealer. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted at 117.25/30 yen against 117.25/35 yen in late New York. It is forecast to trade in a range of 116.90-117.90 yen in Tokyo on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030527dz5r017tu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
