\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar steadies, supported by wariness of BOJ. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 568 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Mai 2003\par 09:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, May 23 (Reuters) - The dollar held steady against the euro and the yen on Friday, hesitating after falling towards launch levels against the euro earlier this week and finding support from wariness of Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell the yen. \par \par \uc2  Concern persists about the U.S. economy and about the extent of Washington's commitment to a strong dollar, but dealers were reluctant to trade heavily ahead of the long weekend in New York and London, where markets will be closed on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers were also looking to German regional inflation data due later for an indication of price growth in the euro zone's largest economy and clues to the next interest rate move from the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "We've been really consolidative this week," said Aziz McMahon, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN Amro. \par \par \uc2  "Expectations for a rate cut from the ECB are there, but the market has got used to that risk." \par \par \uc2  The euro was quoted at $1.1717 at 0730 GMT, compared with its late U.S. level of $1.1694/00. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted at 117.22/25 yen, steady from the U.S. close but off a two-week high of 117.78 yen hit on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  EURO PROFIT-TAKING \par \par \uc2  Investors have been bagging profits on the euro since it hit a four-year high around $1.1744 on Wednesday, just shy of its January 1999 launch level of $1.1747, where massive options-related offers were said to be lined up. \par \par \uc2  "Euro/dollar is vulnerable to a correction after it failed to get above $1.1740, and speculation of a euro zone rate cut on June 5 is likely to intensify," said Ian Stannard, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BNP Paribas. \par \par \uc2  Five German states - Bavaria, Saxony, Brandenburg, Baden-Wuerttemberg and North Rhine-Westphalia - publish inflation data on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Data on Thursday showed the Hesse CPI fell 0.2 percent on the month in May, a trend that if followed throughout the country could push German inflation to well below 1.0 percent. The data boosted expectations the ECB may cut rates in June. \par \par \uc2  Spanish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Jaime Caruana said on Friday the euro zone inflation outlook had improved considerably, and the ECB would take the improved outlook into account in its decisions. \par \par \uc2  The euro hit its highest since August 2001 against the Swiss franc above 1.52 francs, after Swiss National Bank chairman Jean-Pierre Roth said late on Thursday the franc was no longer a safe haven. \par \par \uc2  The greenback hit a two-year low of 115.10 yen on Monday, mainly triggered by comments from U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow that recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements had been "fairly modest". \par \par \uc2  Although U.S. officials said the United States was sticking to its strong dollar policy, Snow's comments reinforced the view that Washington was comfortable with a weaker dollar. \par \par \uc2  Investors remain wary of covert \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by Japanese authorities, with dealers saying there has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's top financial diplomat, Zembei Mizoguchi, said on Friday that an excessive rise in the yen against the dollar was a concern for Japanese companies even though the yen has fallen to record lows against the euro. \par \par \uc2  Recent data shows \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is nursing a fragile export-led recovery, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the January-March quarter to depress the yen. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030523dz5n00fwr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
